WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.720
Welcome to DBL Group’s TalentHub!

2
00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:07.001
This video is for the Factory HR team.

3
00:00:07.121 --> 00:00:10.960
You have three main
responsibilities in TalentHub.

4
00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:13.040
Let’s go through them one by one.

5
00:00:13.390 --> 00:00:16.310
First,

6
00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:20.230
when a new requisition
is created in your unit,

7
00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:25.710
it comes to you for Job Analysis
before entering the Approval Process.

8
00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:32.150
Second, once the job posting is published,

9
00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:36.320
you’ll forward collected
CVs to the recruiter.

10
00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:40.260
Third, you’ll conduct the first interview
for candidates assigned by the recruiter.

11
00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:45.340
Factory HR access is assigned by unit.
If you need new access,

12
00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:50.340
contact the Head of Talent Acquisition.
When multiple Factory HR

13
00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:56.700
users are assigned to the same unit, they
can work from the same Job Analysis queue.

14
00:00:57.050 --> 00:01:02.371
Sign in using your official
DBL Group email and password.

15
00:01:02.491 --> 00:01:07.091
For your first login, use your
Employee Code as the initial password.

16
00:01:07.211 --> 00:01:10.010
After signing in, set your own password.

17
00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:15.440
Use Requisitions in the sidebar
to complete Job Analysis.

18
00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:20.160
When recruiters assign candidates, you’ll
find them under Assigned Candidates.

19
00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:24.480
My Interviews contains
your interview details.

20
00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:28.240
Beside the Bell icon is
the Availability button,

21
00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:30.840
which you can use when going on leave.

22
00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:36.390
Let’s begin with Job Analysis. When a new
requisition is submitted in your unit,

23
00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:41.350
the assigned Factory HR
members receive notifications,

24
00:01:41.470 --> 00:01:45.830
and any of them can begin working on it.

25
00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:49.910
Open the requisition with Job Analysis
status from the Requisitions menu.

26
00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:54.300
The Job Analysis tab
contains two sections.

27
00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:57.870
Section A displays the information
provided by the Requisition Raiser.

28
00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:01.836
Section B contains four
fields for you to complete.

29
00:02:01.956 --> 00:02:08.020
Last worked on by shows who most
recently worked on the requisition.

30
00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:11.890
If any information in
Section A needs correction,

31
00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:14.970
click Edit vacancy information.

32
00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:21.410
You can update the position,
department, number of posts, or dates.

33
00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:27.410
All changes are recorded in History
without affecting the Approval Chain.

34
00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:30.760
Now let’s begin the Job Analysis,

35
00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:33.213
with assistance from AI.

36
00:02:33.333 --> 00:02:38.200
Click Draft with AI,

37
00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:42.020
and the system analyzes the requisition
to generate drafts for four fields:

38
00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:47.800
Job Description, Education & Training,
Experience, and Others.

39
00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:53.040
Before submitting, carefully review
and update the information as needed.

40
00:02:53.390 --> 00:02:56.965
Enter the position’s key duties and
responsibilities under Job Description,

41
00:02:57.085 --> 00:02:59.735
educational qualifications
under Education & Training,

42
00:02:59.855 --> 00:03:05.830
required experience under Experience,
and additional conditions under Others.

43
00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:10.830
For this example, we’re adding
information to the Experience field.

44
00:03:11.180 --> 00:03:15.300
If you need to attach
additional documents,

45
00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:20.900
upload them as PDFs through Attachments.
Make sure to add them before submission,

46
00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:24.300
as new files cannot be uploaded afterward.

47
00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:28.770
You can save your progress
and continue later. You or another

48
00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:34.490
Factory HR member from your unit can
resume the work from where it was saved.

49
00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:40.960
If the requisition requires corrections
from the raiser, use Return to raiser.

50
00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:46.960
Explain the required changes in
the comments and click Send back.

51
00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:51.200
Once the Requisition Raiser makes
the corrections and resubmits,

52
00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:54.600
it returns to your Job Analysis queue.

53
00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:59.470
After reviewing all information,
click Submit for approval.

54
00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:02.591
The requisition status
changes to Pending Approval,

55
00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:06.390
and the first approver in the Approval
Chain receives a notification.

56
00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:12.060
If a unit has no assigned Factory HR
or all Factory HR members are Away,

57
00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:13.980
the Head of Talent Acquisition

58
00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:18.740
and Corporate Recruiters
can handle the Job Analysis.

59
00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:22.750
Now let’s move to the second task:
sending CVs to recruiters.

60
00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:27.690
Once a job posting is published, you’ll
find Send CVs to the recruiter under the

61
00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:31.960
requisition’s Profile & Posting tab. This
section also provides the Public Job Link,

62
00:04:32.530 --> 00:04:37.730
Share job link, and Social post options.

63
00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:41.080
Before sending CVs,

64
00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:45.053
select the Source to indicate
where they were collected.

65
00:04:45.173 --> 00:04:49.360
For Employee Referral,
also select the employee who

66
00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:51.600
referred the candidate.

67
00:04:51.950 --> 00:04:55.590
Upload the candidates’ CVs as PDF files.

68
00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:59.030
You can add up to 30 CVs at once.

69
00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:02.870
Candidate names are automatically
extracted from the file names.

70
00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:07.150
Review and correct them if needed,
then click Send CVs.

71
00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:12.820
Once submitted, the CVs reach the
recruiter with Applied status.

72
00:05:12.940 --> 00:05:15.540
The list below shows the
candidates you’ve submitted

73
00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:19.140
and their previous application counts.

74
00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:23.020
The recruiter then handles
the next stage of screening.

75
00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:28.130
Now let’s move to the third task:
conducting candidates’ first interviews.

76
00:05:28.250 --> 00:05:32.850
When recruiters send candidates for
interviews, you’ll receive a notification.

77
00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:36.690
Their details will
then appear under Assigned Candidates,

78
00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:40.330
where only candidates
assigned to you are displayed.

79
00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:42.560
There are five columns.

80
00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:47.520
To Schedule means the
interview time hasn’t been set.

81
00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:52.000
Scheduled means the
interview has been arranged.

82
00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:57.568
Decision Due means the
interview is complete

83
00:05:57.688 --> 00:06:03.328
but a decision is pending.

84
00:06:03.448 --> 00:06:06.798
With HR Head means the candidate
is awaiting the HR Head’s decision.

85
00:06:06.918 --> 00:06:10.520
Done means this stage has been completed.

86
00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:15.310
You can schedule interviews for
multiple candidates at once.

87
00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:19.389
For this example,
we’re selecting two candidates.

88
00:06:19.509 --> 00:06:25.390
Then click Schedule 2 selected. If no
candidates are selected individually,

89
00:06:25.510 --> 00:06:30.470
you can use Schedule all to
schedule everyone together.

90
00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:36.940
Set the interview date and time using
Bangladesh Standard Time. For online

91
00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:41.953
interviews, the system automatically
generates a Google Meet link.

92
00:06:42.073 --> 00:06:48.340
For in-person interviews, select the
Location and enter the room name.

93
00:06:48.690 --> 00:06:51.940
The Interview Panel is divided
into two groups: From HR Department

94
00:06:52.060 --> 00:06:57.050
and From other departments. HR panelists
can also enter the candidate’s Salary

95
00:06:57.170 --> 00:07:01.090
and Benefits information.

96
00:07:01.210 --> 00:07:05.510
Below, you’ll find Google Calendar
and Email options for candidates,

97
00:07:05.630 --> 00:07:10.332
along with Calendar and Email
notifications for panel members.

98
00:07:10.452 --> 00:07:15.330
Review the details and click Schedule.

99
00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:19.800
On the interview day, the candidate’s
card displays Did this interview happen?

100
00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:25.080
Select Interviewed if the
candidate attended or Did not

101
00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:31.200
attend if they were absent. However,
once a panelist has submitted marks,

102
00:07:31.320 --> 00:07:35.680
the Did not attend option
is no longer available.

103
00:07:36.030 --> 00:07:40.630
If you need to change the interview time,
you can reschedule it.

104
00:07:40.750 --> 00:07:46.230
The candidate receives both the previous
and updated interview times by email,

105
00:07:46.670 --> 00:07:49.870
while the Interview Panel
links remain unchanged.

106
00:07:50.220 --> 00:07:53.920
You can enter marks for two tests:
Written Test and Computer Literacy Test.

107
00:07:54.040 --> 00:07:59.140
AI Proficiency Test marks
are automatically provided

108
00:07:59.260 --> 00:08:03.700
by the system based on the
candidate’s assessment results.

109
00:08:03.820 --> 00:08:06.820
Enter the applicable test marks.

110
00:08:06.940 --> 00:08:11.780
Once saved or submitted,
the marks are locked for you.

111
00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:17.420
Contact the recruiter if
corrections are needed.

112
00:08:17.770 --> 00:08:23.650
Once the Interview Panel
has submitted the marks,

113
00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:28.771
the candidate moves to Decision Due.
Click Decide to provide your decision.

114
00:08:28.891 --> 00:08:34.291
Selecting Yes sends the candidate to
the unit’s HR Head for approval, if one

115
00:08:34.651 --> 00:08:39.370
is assigned. Otherwise, the candidate
proceeds directly to the Final Interview.

116
00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:44.320
If you don’t want to move a
candidate to the next stage,

117
00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:49.520
select No and provide a reason.
Selecting Also send the regret

118
00:08:49.640 --> 00:08:54.437
mail sends DBL Group’s Regret
Letter to the candidate by email.

119
00:08:54.787 --> 00:08:58.427
To send multiple candidates
to the HR Head together,

120
00:08:58.547 --> 00:09:02.347
use Send finalists to HR Head.

121
00:09:02.467 --> 00:09:06.347
The HR Head receives all candidate
details in a single email

122
00:09:06.467 --> 00:09:08.947
and can provide decisions from there.

123
00:09:09.297 --> 00:09:11.737
Now let’s look at the
Availability feature.

124
00:09:12.257 --> 00:09:16.777
The round button beside the Bell icon
shows green when you’re Available

125
00:09:16.897 --> 00:09:18.937
and amber when you’re Away.

126
00:09:19.057 --> 00:09:25.017
Before going on leave, click it
and select three, seven, or fifteen days.

127
00:09:25.777 --> 00:09:30.537
You can also set a custom
end date and add a note.

128
00:09:31.297 --> 00:09:33.777
Then click Confirm leave.

129
00:09:34.127 --> 00:09:39.927
While you’re Away, you’re temporarily
removed from the Job Analysis queue.

130
00:09:40.047 --> 00:09:44.407
You won’t receive new Job
Analysis notifications,

131
00:09:44.527 --> 00:09:48.847
and pending tasks won’t
appear in your list.

132
00:09:48.967 --> 00:09:53.007
Other Factory HR members in
your unit can continue working.

133
00:09:53.357 --> 00:09:56.997
If you return before your leave ends,
click the Availability button

134
00:09:57.117 --> 00:10:01.477
and select I’m back. Otherwise,
the system automatically

135
00:10:01.597 --> 00:10:06.077
changes your status to Available
when your leave period ends.

136
00:10:06.427 --> 00:10:10.227
You’ll receive notifications when a new
requisition arrives for Job Analysis,

137
00:10:10.347 --> 00:10:13.427
a Requisition Raiser resubmits
a corrected requisition,

138
00:10:13.547 --> 00:10:19.347
a recruiter assigns candidates,
or the HR Head provides a decision.

139
00:10:19.707 --> 00:10:24.027
You’ll also receive updates when
interviews are scheduled or rescheduled.

140
00:10:24.377 --> 00:10:27.777
To receive notifications by email,
go to the Notifications

141
00:10:27.897 --> 00:10:31.417
tab under Settings
and keep Email notifications enabled.

142
00:10:31.767 --> 00:10:36.607
Can you complete a Job Analysis
started by a colleague? Yes.

143
00:10:37.447 --> 00:10:43.487
Factory HR members from the same unit can
continue each other’s work when needed.

144
00:10:43.607 --> 00:10:49.487
Last worked on by shows who
worked on it most recently,

145
00:10:49.607 --> 00:10:55.127
while all changes are recorded in History.

146
00:10:55.477 --> 00:10:59.997
New attachments cannot be added
after Job Analysis submission.

147
00:11:00.597 --> 00:11:03.117
If additional documents are required,

148
00:11:03.237 --> 00:11:06.397
contact the Head of Talent Acquisition.

149
00:11:07.157 --> 00:11:11.997
Similarly, for corrections
to submitted test marks,

150
00:11:12.117 --> 00:11:15.157
contact the recruiter
or the Head of Talent Acquisition.

151
00:11:15.507 --> 00:11:17.307
Let’s quickly recap.

152
00:11:17.427 --> 00:11:21.454
First, complete Job
Analysis under Requisitions.

153
00:11:21.574 --> 00:11:25.360
Use Draft with AI to prepare
the information, review it,

154
00:11:25.480 --> 00:11:27.427
and click Submit for approval.

155
00:11:27.777 --> 00:11:30.663
Second, use Profile & Posting to select

156
00:11:30.783 --> 00:11:34.337
the CV Source
and forward CVs to the recruiter.

157
00:11:34.687 --> 00:11:38.487
Third, use Assigned Candidates
to schedule interviews,

158
00:11:38.607 --> 00:11:43.007
confirm attendance,
and provide candidate decisions.

159
00:11:43.357 --> 00:11:47.077
Remember to update your
Availability before going on leave.

160
00:11:47.837 --> 00:11:51.397
The complete guide is available
as a PDF under Tutorials.

161
00:11:51.997 --> 00:11:58.277
For login-related issues,
contact the IT Helpdesk.

162
00:11:58.397 --> 00:12:01.597
Thank you for using DBL Group’s TalentHub.

